    "dynamic_instructions": "{\r\n  \"datasetView\": \"**Train Tree 2**\\n\\nGoal: Train a new tree on the (Fixed) dataset. Compare it to Tree 1.\\n\\n1. Read the **Dataset Update** below.\\n2. In **Predict**, choose your label. In **Using**, keep your two features, or add more.\\n3. Click **Train model**.\\n\\nYou are done when your tree shows. Go to the **Testing** tab.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Dataset Update**: \\n\\nAdds five fruits that are high in natural sugar.\\n\\n**Data Source**: \\n\\nReal foods from USDA FoodData Central, SR Legacy (April 2018 release), https://fdc.nal.usda.gov. Source: USDA FoodData Central\",\r\n  \"results\": \"**Train Tree 2**\\n\\nGoal: Train a new tree on the (Fixed) dataset. Compare it to Tree 1.\\n\\n1. Copy your Tree 1 label, features, Accuracy and correct test records from Lesson 12 into the Tree 1 row of **Tree 1 vs. Tree 2** in your guide.\\n2. Find your **Accuracy** at the top. Write it in the Tree 2 row.\\n3. Click **Accuracy**. Write how many test records are **Correct**, out of all the test records.\\n4. Write the label and features you used for Tree 2.\\n5. Click **Save image** (the camera under your tree). Click **Save to Backpack**.\\n\\nYou are done when Tree 1 vs. Tree 2 in your guide is full and Tree 2 is in your Backpack.\"\r\n}",
